From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] loader: clear the scratch trailer on a degenerate
 copy_size == 0 swap

boot_swap_image() hands copy_size to swap_run() unconditionally.  With the
scratch algorithm (swap_scratch.c), copy_size == 0 makes
find_last_sector_idx() return -1 (its break condition
`primary_slot_size >= copy_size && secondary_slot_size >= copy_size &&
primary_slot_size == secondary_slot_size` is satisfied immediately at
0 >= 0 && 0 >= 0 && 0 == 0), so swap_run()'s
`while (last_sector_idx >= 0)` loop body never runs.  boot_swap_sectors() --
and with it the scratch-trailer erase at swap_scratch.c's
`boot_scramble_region(fap_scratch, ...)` -- is only ever called from inside
that loop, so it is never reached either.

On a flash device whose reported erase value is 0x00 (Alif Ensemble on-die
MRAM, drivers/flash/flash_mram_alif.c FLASH_MRAM_ERASE_VALUE), that erase
value is bit-for-bit identical to a genuine swap_size of 0.
boot_read_swap_size() is a raw, unchecked read, so a stale or
partially-written trailer field reads back as copy_size == 0 in the resume
branch instead of the obviously-invalid 0xffffffff a 0xFF-erase device
would show; a scratch magic left over from an earlier attempt then keeps
reading GOOD.  boot_status_source()'s boot_status_tables[2]
(magic_primary=ANY, magic_scratch=GOOD -> BOOT_STATUS_SOURCE_SCRATCH)
selects the scratch source on every following boot regardless of
image_ok, so the board resumes the same no-op swap forever: it never moves
a byte, and it never clears the scratch magic that put it there.

Guard the call site instead of the swap algorithm: if copy_size is 0,
clear the scratch trailer directly (the same boot_scramble_region() call
swap_run()'s loop would have performed had it actually executed) and
reset the boot status, rather than resuming a swap that can never
complete.  This is a no-op for the common case -- a real swap-in-progress
trailer never carries copy_size == 0 -- and is scoped to
MCUBOOT_SWAP_USING_SCRATCH, so move/offset builds are unaffected.

Bug: a swapped board on a no-erase-value-0x00 device re-swaps on every
subsequent boot because the scratch magic is never cleared.

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
index 6edb298..725b8c8 100644
--- a/boot/bootutil/src/loader.c
+++ b/boot/bootutil/src/loader.c
@@ -1224,6 +1224,37 @@ boot_swap_image(struct boot_loader_state *state, struct boot_status *bs)
         flash_area_close(fap);
     }
 
+#if MCUBOOT_SWAP_USING_SCRATCH
+    if (copy_size == 0) {
+        /*
+         * copy_size == 0 makes swap_run()'s scratch algorithm degenerate
+         * into a no-op: find_last_sector_idx() returns -1, so the loop that
+         * calls boot_swap_sectors() -- and with it the scratch-trailer
+         * erase at its tail -- never runs. On a flash device whose erase
+         * value is 0x00 (e.g. Alif Ensemble on-die MRAM), that erase value
+         * is bit-for-bit identical to a genuine swap_size of 0, so a stale
+         * or partially-written trailer field reads back as copy_size == 0
+         * instead of the obviously-invalid 0xffffffff a 0xFF-erase device
+         * would show. Left unhandled, the scratch trailer's magic is never
+         * cleared, boot_status_source() keeps selecting
+         * BOOT_STATUS_SOURCE_SCRATCH on every following boot, and the board
+         * re-enters this same branch forever -- a swap that "completes"
+         * without ever moving a byte.
+         *
+         * Clear the scratch trailer directly (the cleanup swap_run() would
+         * have performed had its loop actually executed) instead of
+         * resuming a swap that can never complete.
+         */
+        BOOT_LOG_ERR("boot_swap_image: copy_size == 0 (degenerate/corrupt "
+                     "swap status); clearing scratch trailer instead of "
+                     "resuming a no-op swap");
+        boot_scramble_region(state->scratch.area, 0,
+                              flash_area_get_size(state->scratch.area), true);
+        boot_status_reset(bs);
+        return 0;
+    }
+#endif
+
     swap_run(state, bs, copy_size);
 
 #ifdef MCUBOOT_VALIDATE_PRIMARY_SLOT
